# How long each step takes

Two numbers per step. The **median** is the typical claim. The **90th percentile** is the slow tail: the wait that 1 claim in 10 exceeds at that step.

chart hbar times y=median,slow tail unit=d labels title="Days per step: median (typical) vs 90th percentile (slow tail)"

!! Do not add up the Median column and call it the wait. Medians do not add into a median for the whole claim, and nobody experiences the typical time at every step. Adding the medians gives about 10 days from first notice to payment for a claim under $10,000 (about 12 with supervisor approval, about 14 to 16 through closure). A claim that lands in the slow tail at just three steps (field inspection 11.5 days, supervisor approval 9.8, estimate and scope 7.1) can wait about 28 days. Percentiles cannot be added at all; that example only shows how fast the tails stack up.

Customers feel the tail. Satisfaction is 71 for claims finished in under 14 days and 38 for claims that take more than 30 days.

data csat = group,satisfaction score; Under 14 days,71; Over 30 days,38

chart bar csat y=satisfaction score labels title="Customer satisfaction by total claim time (score)"

